1
00:00:11,759 --> 00:00:14,279
Let me introduce you two.

2
00:00:14,759 --> 00:00:17,079
This is a top Whampoa Military Academy graduate,

3
00:00:17,079 --> 00:00:17,879
Li Mingyuan.

4
00:00:18,559 --> 00:00:19,879
Ever since he joined the department,

5
00:00:19,879 --> 00:00:21,000
he's solved one major case after another,

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,920
making him our finest asset here.

7
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,039
Mingyuan,

8
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,879
Xu Jie has only been here for six months,

9
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,000
but...

10
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:30,600
he's the sharpest lad in our department.

11
00:00:30,879 --> 00:00:31,600
Starting today,

12
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,880
you'll be taking him under your wing.

13
00:00:35,079 --> 00:00:35,640
All right.

14
00:00:36,479 --> 00:00:36,920
Mentor.

15
00:01:07,319 --> 00:01:08,079
I'll take you to the hospital.

16
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,920
Mentor... Mentor...

17
00:01:13,599 --> 00:01:14,359
It was him, wasn't it?

18
00:01:15,319 --> 00:01:16,480
He forced you, right?

19
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:18,680
Mentor...

20
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,760
Mentor, I'm sorry.

21
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,640
I didn't want to do that.

22
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:25,239
I wanted to be a good cop.

23
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,719
You've always done well.

24
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:30,640
If only...

25
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:34,439
If only you'd been my mentor from the start.

26
00:02:03,959 --> 00:02:05,400
A Browning 1900.

27
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,719
A very common pistol.

28
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,280
There's something off about this bullet.

29
00:02:25,919 --> 00:02:26,599
This bullet...

30
00:02:27,039 --> 00:02:28,919
seems to be for a Type 38 rifle.

31
00:02:31,639 --> 00:02:32,719
6.5 mm caliber,

32
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:35,479
75.70 mm in length.

33
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,719
That's right. A Type 38 rifle.

34
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,080
The Japanese military's primary combat weapon.

35
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:50,280
Alright.

36
00:02:50,919 --> 00:02:52,800
This is the police station's main office.

37
00:02:53,319 --> 00:02:55,439
Upstairs are the archives, meeting rooms,

38
00:02:55,439 --> 00:02:56,479
and the Chief's office.

39
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:57,479
Let me show you around.

40
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:02,479
This is the police department's top detective,

41
00:03:02,639 --> 00:03:03,560
Captain Li Mingyuan.

42
00:03:04,599 --> 00:03:05,400
Hello, Captain Li.

43
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:09,879
Let's go.

44
00:03:27,759 --> 00:03:30,400
A few officers at Rongcheng Police Station got drunk today

45
00:03:30,879 --> 00:03:31,960
and talked about the Lian family's case.

46
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:35,639
Two years ago, Uncle Lian was in a car accident.

47
00:03:36,199 --> 00:03:38,439
The case was quickly closed as an accident,

48
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:42,319
but there's actually a confidential file at the station.

49
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,199
It contains information on the officers

50
00:03:44,199 --> 00:03:45,639
and everyone involved.

51
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:48,039
With this file,

52
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,960
we might find the real killer

53
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,039
of Uncle and Aunt Lian.

54
00:04:05,199 --> 00:04:06,080
I knew it was you.

55
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:07,680
What are you doing here?

56
00:04:08,479 --> 00:04:09,120
What are you doing here?

57
00:04:16,639 --> 00:04:17,360
Let go of me!

58
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,439
You first.

59
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,360
Why did you sneak into the police station?

60
00:04:23,199 --> 00:04:23,920
Regarding my family's case,

61
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,319
there's a confidential file kept here.

62
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:27,759
I just want to see it.

63
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,639
Unauthorized personnel

64
00:04:35,759 --> 00:04:37,480
aren't allowed into the archives to view files.

65
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:43,439
Just let me take a lo—

66
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:45,360
Listen to me.

67
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,920
Officers patrol the archives on a regular schedule.

68
00:04:48,519 --> 00:04:49,959
If you don't want to get riddled with bullets,

69
00:04:50,879 --> 00:04:51,680
get out of here right now.

70
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:55,800
Right.

71
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:58,079
You're right.

72
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,240
Then I'll leave.

73
00:05:00,439 --> 00:05:00,920
Leave?

74
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,279
Hand it over.

75
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,240
Three.

76
00:05:14,319 --> 00:05:14,879
Here, take it back.

77
00:05:31,839 --> 00:05:32,519
Dr. Hao,

78
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:36,240
how long will it take for him to recover?

79
00:05:36,879 --> 00:05:38,519
Acupuncture is only a supplementary treatment.

80
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,839
A sickness of the heart needs medicine for the mind.

81
00:05:41,199 --> 00:05:41,920
Just take it slow.

82
00:05:43,839 --> 00:05:44,600
Shuisheng.

83
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,959
Brother Lian has a few questions for you.

84
00:05:48,439 --> 00:05:50,000
That night...

85
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,000
the group of people you saw...

86
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,120
No.

87
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,399
The ghosts you saw...

88
00:05:58,879 --> 00:06:00,120
inside the coffin they were carrying,

89
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,040
what was inside?

90
00:06:19,639 --> 00:06:20,360
Could it be...

91
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,160
Stop!

92
00:06:31,199 --> 00:06:32,800
The killer wasn't smuggling cloth,

93
00:06:33,319 --> 00:06:34,120
but weapons.

94
00:06:35,759 --> 00:06:38,000
A mole in the police is in cahoots with the Japanese,

95
00:06:38,519 --> 00:06:39,600
covering up the truth for them.

96
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:41,680
A partnership.

97
00:06:43,879 --> 00:06:44,480
Deal.

98
00:06:55,279 --> 00:06:56,480
That man is Sun Changgen.

99
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:58,759
Cousin of Sun Hanji from the Shipboard Guild.

100
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:03,319
That old bastard Sun Hanji really is dirty.

101
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,480
Shen Tieshan

102
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,079
died under suspicious circumstances.

103
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:12,639
Hurry, hurry!

104
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:15,639
No wonder in the Sea Goddess Temple murder,

105
00:07:16,279 --> 00:07:17,480
they chose to hide the body here.

106
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:19,519
What do you mean?

107
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:23,920
Think about it.

108
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,399
A murder happened in Net Cave,

109
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:27,920
so fishermen won't dare come near.

110
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,680
Over time, this place

111
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,920
became completely abandoned.

112
00:07:32,439 --> 00:07:34,879
Perfect for stashing dirty cargo.

113
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:35,759
Killing two birds with one stone.

114
00:07:40,279 --> 00:07:41,319
The situation is complicated now.

115
00:07:41,439 --> 00:07:42,839
If these weapons flow into Rongcheng,

116
00:07:43,199 --> 00:07:43,959
once war breaks out,

117
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:45,399
the consequences will be catastrophic.

118
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,240
What are you doing?

119
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:54,439
Take them out!

120
00:07:55,079 --> 00:07:56,199
They're heavily guarded.

121
00:07:56,199 --> 00:07:56,920
Can't you see?

122
00:07:57,279 --> 00:07:58,519
There are guards posted all around.

123
00:07:58,839 --> 00:07:59,879
Even if you could take on a hundred men,

124
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:01,560
you couldn't survive being swarmed!

125
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:05,040
Then you tell me, what do we do now?

126
00:08:16,639 --> 00:08:17,279
Surround the area!

127
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,720
Captain Li! Captain Li!

128
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,800
Captain Li! Captain Li!

129
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:23,519
What's all this about?

130
00:08:25,959 --> 00:08:27,839
Captain Li, Captain Li, please don't!

131
00:08:27,839 --> 00:08:30,079
Someone reported contraband hidden here.

132
00:08:30,399 --> 00:08:31,279
I must conduct a thorough search.

133
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:32,600
Captain Li...

134
00:08:32,799 --> 00:08:33,720
Don't listen to their nonsense.

135
00:08:33,879 --> 00:08:35,720
There's only some junk in here.

136
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,919
Whether it's junk or not,

137
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,240
we'll know once we take a look.

138
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:38,720
Wait, please don't!

139
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:45,960
Director Zhou.

140
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:47,919
What are you doing here?

141
00:08:48,799 --> 00:08:50,799
Someone reported contraband here.

142
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,240
I've already searched this place with my men.

143
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:55,960
There's nothing illegal.

144
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,320
Take your men and head back.

145
00:08:59,759 --> 00:09:00,559
Yes, Director Zhou.

146
00:09:07,679 --> 00:09:08,240
Pull back!

147
00:09:15,399 --> 00:09:16,120
Director Zhou...

148
00:09:16,679 --> 00:09:17,519
Thank goodness you showed up.

149
00:09:20,919 --> 00:09:21,720
Let me tell you this.

150
00:09:23,039 --> 00:09:24,039
I can help you once,

151
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,200
but not a second time.

152
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,559
This place has been compromised.

153
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,799
Move your goods right now.

154
00:09:31,559 --> 00:09:32,000
Yes, sir.

155
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,360
Quick, quick! Hurry up!

156
00:09:44,639 --> 00:09:45,360
Move, move, move!

157
00:09:46,519 --> 00:09:47,399
Quick! Over here!

158
00:09:47,399 --> 00:09:49,080
Brother Lian, what are they doing?

159
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:50,679
Shut up.

160
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:51,960
Follow them.

161
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,639
Move it, move it! Hurry!

162
00:10:02,039 --> 00:10:03,960
You two, take them and keep watch inside.

163
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,120
The rest of you, follow me!

164
00:10:05,279 --> 00:10:06,039
Yes, sir! Right away!

165
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:33,399
Open the crates.

166
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:46,200
Brother Lian,

167
00:10:46,799 --> 00:10:48,240
they're all Japanese Type 38 rifles!

168
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,200
We hit the jackpot!

169
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:57,120
Take them all back.

170
00:10:58,279 --> 00:10:58,799
Yes, sir!

171
00:11:11,679 --> 00:11:13,080
Brother Lian, everything is ready.

172
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,480
We can't carry off the rest of the gunpowder,

173
00:11:24,159 --> 00:11:25,559
but are we really going to blow it up just like that?

174
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:30,840
Blow it up.

175
00:11:32,639 --> 00:11:33,759
Leaving it behind will only cause trouble.

176
00:11:38,759 --> 00:11:39,799
Where are the guns?

177
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:43,679
Where's the shipment?

178
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:45,960
Where the hell did you put the shipment?

179
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:48,000
It was all locked in the warehouse last night!

180
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:48,559
Mr. Matsui...

181
00:11:48,879 --> 00:11:49,279
It was all here...

182
00:11:54,399 --> 00:11:55,200
Sun Hanji!

183
00:11:55,679 --> 00:11:56,879
At all costs,

184
00:11:57,399 --> 00:11:58,759
track down every last bit of that shipment!

185
00:11:59,360 --> 00:11:59,960
U-Understood!

186
00:12:08,399 --> 00:12:09,039
Cheers!

187
00:12:14,399 --> 00:12:15,600
What's got you so thrilled?

188
00:12:16,279 --> 00:12:17,080
A windfall fell right into our laps!

189
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,399
We hit the jackpot this time.

190
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:30,440
Brother Mingyuan, it's rare to see you here.

191
00:12:30,879 --> 00:12:31,600
What tea would you like?

192
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:32,919
Yongtai green tea.

193
00:12:40,679 --> 00:12:41,879
Where did you stash the goods?

194
00:12:47,759 --> 00:12:48,440
What goods?

195
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,000
You're going back on your word!

196
00:12:54,399 --> 00:12:55,000
How about this?

197
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:57,039
Tomorrow, I'll take the Sanshan Gang boys

198
00:12:57,039 --> 00:12:58,399
and seize that arms shipment in one sweep.

199
00:12:58,399 --> 00:12:58,919
No way.

200
00:12:59,639 --> 00:13:00,480
They're heavily guarded.

201
00:13:01,039 --> 00:13:01,720
If you try to take it by force,

202
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,279
it'll be a pyrrhic victory.

203
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,519
Besides, let me remind you,

204
00:13:04,519 --> 00:13:06,440
this case is police business.

205
00:13:07,919 --> 00:13:09,240
Xu Jie was a cautionary tale.

206
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,720
Can your police department even be trusted?

207
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,159
Chief Song

208
00:13:16,159 --> 00:13:17,279
is about to retire,

209
00:13:17,759 --> 00:13:18,639
so he won't get involved.

210
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,159
Even if you manage

211
00:13:20,159 --> 00:13:22,039
to move the weapons to the station today,

212
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:23,919
the mole will find a way

213
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,559
to swap them back

214
00:13:25,559 --> 00:13:26,480
untouched tomorrow.

215
00:13:27,279 --> 00:13:28,879
It'll all be for nothing.

216
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:32,919
Here's the plan.

217
00:13:33,519 --> 00:13:34,879
Tomorrow, I'll stage a raid

218
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:35,759
to flush them out

219
00:13:36,559 --> 00:13:37,559
and make them move the weapons.

220
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:38,919
You make your move then.

221
00:13:43,559 --> 00:13:44,000
Brilliant.

222
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:47,799
Right.

223
00:13:47,919 --> 00:13:49,919
Now, I agreed to work with you,

224
00:13:49,919 --> 00:13:51,600
but I never promised

225
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:53,639
I'd hand the weapons over to you.

226
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,799
Right, they belong to us!

227
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,000
We won't hand them over.

228
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:00,919
Snap out of it!

229
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:03,080
The mastermind will soon realize

230
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:03,919
that you have them.

231
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:04,799
These weapons—

232
00:14:04,799 --> 00:14:05,960
everyone has their eye on them.

233
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:08,120
You won't survive attacks from all sides.

234
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:10,840
These arms aren't a prize to you,

235
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,519
they're a hot potato!

236
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:15,120
It's not too late to turn them over to me.

237
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:17,200
I promise they'll be kept in a safe place.

238
00:14:18,559 --> 00:14:19,799
You've been nagging forever.

239
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:20,720
I know all that.

240
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:22,919
You did this on purpose.

241
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:24,720
You used me to seize the guns on purpose,

242
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,679
drawing dangerous heat right onto yourself!

243
00:14:26,879 --> 00:14:27,879
What the hell are you after?

244
00:14:27,879 --> 00:14:28,840
Painting a giant target on your back...

245
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:30,039
You won't even see your death coming!

246
00:14:30,759 --> 00:14:32,080
Don't trouble yourself over me.

247
00:14:32,399 --> 00:14:33,039
Brother Mingyuan.

248
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:34,399
Where are the goods?

249
00:14:35,039 --> 00:14:35,840
You can have them,

250
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,440
on one condition.

251
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,120
Name it.

252
00:14:43,879 --> 00:14:45,120
Trade them for my parents' case files.

253
00:14:47,559 --> 00:14:48,200
Impossible.

254
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:49,919
Then see yourself out.

255
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,600
Brother Mingyuan, why leave so soon?

256
00:14:53,039 --> 00:14:54,000
You haven't even touched your tea.

257
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,000
You...

258
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,120
The armory exploded,

259
00:15:13,679 --> 00:15:15,600
and over a thousand rifles vanished.

260
00:15:16,759 --> 00:15:18,679
Find a way to get those guns back for me.

261
00:15:21,159 --> 00:15:22,759
Yes, Mr. Matsui.

262
00:15:37,039 --> 00:15:37,879
Regarding my family's case,

263
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:40,159
there's a confidential file kept here.

264
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:41,600
I want to see it.

265
00:15:43,879 --> 00:15:44,440
Where are the goods?

266
00:15:45,399 --> 00:15:46,600
Trade them for my parents' case files.
